# November 24, 2026: a third scatter across Oregon, claimed with tools/choose.py --thinnest (region or, 47 places when the
# session began). Ten places in nine counties: a canal lock system, a utopian colony, two coast lighthouses, an army fort
# site, a homestead village, a pioneer farm, a woolen mill, a sea captain's mansion and a 1914 school. Facts come from
# Wikipedia read with tools/wiki_raw.py and from the pages of whoever runs each place where one could be read (the Old
# Aurora Colony Museum, the Willamette Heritage Center, the Philip Foster Farm, the Willamette Falls Locks, Oregon State
# Parks). Hours that could only be read as a web search result quotes them are marked so in the access note.
